IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Delaware Code, Title 31, Chapter 5 (State Public Assistance Code), with the Delaware Social Services Manual 4000 (16 Del.
-- Admin. Code 4000) that s 503(d) leaves to set eligibility and the amount -- Temporary Assistance for Needy Families (TANF):
-- the bars in s 503(a) (a transfer without fair consideration; an inmate of a public institution) and s 503(d) (nonsupport
-- proceedings); the $10,000 resource limit (DSSM 4002.2); earned income and its disregards (DSSM 4004.2, 4004.5, 4004.6);
-- child support (DSSM 4005.1); the standards (DSSM 4007, 4007.2); the gross and net income tests and the Fill the Gap grant
-- (DSSM 4008, 4008.1.1, 4008.1.2); the duty to report new property or income (s 510); and the appeal to the Superior Court
-- (s 520).
--
-- SEAT: the applicant for, or recipient of, TANF (the parent or caretaker who applies for the family). "Does my family pass
-- the income tests? How much would our grant be? What counts and what does not? Must I report new income? Until when can I
-- appeal?" The Department of Health and Social Services (Division of Social Services) appears only as what it must or may do
-- to the family.
--
-- Edition: The Delaware Code Online, Title 31, chapter 5, "includes all acts enacted as of September 10, 2026, up to and
-- including 85 Del. Laws, c. 518", as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/de-code-t31-ch05-2026-09-10.txt; and DSSM 4000
-- as published in the Delaware Administrative Code on 2026-10-19 (latest amendment cited 29 DE Reg. 530 (12/01/25)), as
-- deposited in the sibling subject
-- ../../../delaware-administrative-code-title-16-dssm-4000-financial-responsibility/registers/source-bundle/
-- de-admin-code-16-dssm-4000-financial-responsibility.txt. The regulation is brought in as the instrument that sets the
-- Act's numbers (the 2026-10-18 scope default).
--
-- THE STANDARDS. DSSM 4007.2 prints the table "Current for 10/2002 - 9/30/2003" and DSSM 4007 and 4008 point to a "COLA
-- Administrative Notice" for current standards, which is not deposited. The 4007.2 figures are encoded as the deposited
-- figures; the grant questions also accept the standards as inputs, for a reader who has the current notice. NOTES.md
-- finding 1.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: General Assistance (DSSM 4004.3, 4007.1, 4009), pregnant women (4010), sponsored aliens (4011), the budget
-- group rules (4001, asked as the number of people), resources beyond the limit (4002.1, 4002.3 to 4002.7), step-parent and
-- minor parent's parent income (4005.3, 4005.4), the list of excluded income (4006), the reduced-employment rule (4004.4),
-- the child support supplemental payment (4008.2); technical eligibility, time limits and work rules (DSSM 3000, not
-- deposited); the Department's sanctions (s 518, regulations not deposited).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written from the applicant's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Delaware TANF`

§§ `DSSM 4007.2 -- the standards`

DECLARE `TANF standards` HAS
    `185% of the standard of need` IS A NUMBER
    `standard of need`             IS A NUMBER
    `payment standard`             IS A NUMBER

-- DSSM 4007.2, "Current for 10/2002 - 9/30/2003": number of people in the budget / 185% of the standard of need / standard of
-- need (75% FPL) / payment standard: 1 $1,024 $554 $201; 2 $1,380 $746 $270; 3 $1,737 $939 $338; 4 $2,092 $1,131 $407;
-- 5 $2,447 $1,323 $475; 6 $2,802 $1,515 $544; 7 $3,161 $1,709 $612; 8 $3,516 $1,901 $681. "* Add $355 per person above eight
-- ... ** Add $192 ... *** Add $69 per person above eight in the family."
GIVEN `the number of people in the budget` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `TANF standards`
`the DSSM 4007.2 standards for` `the number of people in the budget` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the number of people in the budget` AT MOST 1 THEN `TANF standards` OF 1024, 554, 201
        IF `the number of people in the budget` EQUALS 2  THEN `TANF standards` OF 1380, 746, 270
        IF `the number of people in the budget` EQUALS 3  THEN `TANF standards` OF 1737, 939, 338
        IF `the number of people in the budget` EQUALS 4  THEN `TANF standards` OF 2092, 1131, 407
        IF `the number of people in the budget` EQUALS 5  THEN `TANF standards` OF 2447, 1323, 475
        IF `the number of people in the budget` EQUALS 6  THEN `TANF standards` OF 2802, 1515, 544
        IF `the number of people in the budget` EQUALS 7  THEN `TANF standards` OF 3161, 1709, 612
        OTHERWISE
            `TANF standards` OF (3516 PLUS 355 TIMES `above eight`), (1901 PLUS 192 TIMES `above eight`), (681 PLUS 69 TIMES `above eight`)
    WHERE
        `above eight` MEANS max 0 (`the number of people in the budget` MINUS 8)

§§ `DSSM 4004 -- earned income and its disregards`

-- DSSM 4004.2: "1. Standard allowance for work connected expenses - $90.00. 2. The $30 plus 1/3 disregard ... the deduction of
-- $30 plus 1/3 of the remaining earned income after the standard allowance ... is subtracted", for four consecutive months;
-- "3. The $30 disregard ... continues to be deducted from earned income for the eight (8) months" after; then neither "until
-- the individual has not received TANF benefits for twelve (12) months". Which stage an earner is in is a fact.
-- "4. Dependent care expenses as paid up to $200 per month per dependent child under age two (2) and up to $175 per month per
-- dependent child or incapacitated adult."
DECLARE `Disregard stage` IS ONE OF
    `in the four months of the $30 plus 1/3 disregard`
    `in the eight months of the $30 disregard`
    `past both disregards`

-- One wage earner in the family. Earnings of dependent children are not entered: DSSM 4004.6 disregards them "without time
-- limits ... in determining the family's eligibility and the amount". EITC payments are not earned income and are disregarded
-- (DSSM 4004.5).
DECLARE `Earner` HAS
    `gross earned income in the month`                        IS A NUMBER
    `disregard stage`                                         IS A `Disregard stage`
    `dependent care paid for children under two`              IS A NUMBER
    `children under two cared for`                            IS A NUMBER
    `dependent care paid for other children or incapacitated adults` IS A NUMBER
    `other children or incapacitated adults cared for`        IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `e` IS AN `Earner`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the dependent care deduction for` `e` MEANS
        min (`e`'s `dependent care paid for children under two`) (200 TIMES `e`'s `children under two cared for`)
    PLUS min (`e`'s `dependent care paid for other children or incapacitated adults`) (175 TIMES `e`'s `other children or incapacitated adults cared for`)

-- The $30 and 1/3 disregards in the stage the earner is in, after the $90.
GIVEN `e` IS AN `Earner`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the $30 and one-third disregards for` `e` MEANS
    CONSIDER `e`'s `disregard stage`
    WHEN `in the four months of the $30 plus 1/3 disregard` THEN
        min `after the $90` (30 PLUS (max 0 (`after the $90` MINUS 30)) DIVIDED BY 3)
    WHEN `in the eight months of the $30 disregard` THEN min `after the $90` 30
    WHEN `past both disregards` THEN 0
    WHERE
        `after the $90` MEANS max 0 (`e`'s `gross earned income in the month` MINUS 90)

-- DSSM 4008.1.1 Step 2 (the applicant net income test): "Subtract the earned income deduction ($90.00) and child care expenses
-- from each wage earner's earnings."
GIVEN `e` IS AN `Earner`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the applicant-test net earnings of` `e` MEANS
    max 0 (`e`'s `gross earned income in the month` MINUS 90 MINUS `the dependent care deduction for` `e`)

-- DSSM 4008.1.1 Step 3 and 4008.1.2 Step 2: "subtract the standard work deduction ($90.00), and 30 plus 1/3 disregard (if
-- applicable) from each earner's earned income, and child care."
GIVEN `e` IS AN `Earner`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the net earnings after all disregards of` `e` MEANS
    max 0 (   `e`'s `gross earned income in the month`
           MINUS 90
           MINUS `the $30 and one-third disregards for` `e`
           MINUS `the dependent care deduction for` `e`)

§§ `The family's month`

DECLARE `TANF family` HAS
    `number of people in the budget`                         IS A NUMBER
    `an applicant, not a recipient`                          IS A BOOLEAN  -- no assistance in any of the four months before applying
    `earners`                                                IS A LIST OF `Earner`
    `unearned income other than child support`               IS A NUMBER
    `child support received in the month`                    IS A NUMBER
    `available resources`                                    IS A NUMBER
    `transferred property worth $500 or more without fair consideration within 2 years before applying, or since` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an inmate of a public institution, other than a patient in a medical institution` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has sued for nonsupport or cooperates with the Department to do so` IS A BOOLEAN

-- DSSM 4005.1: "the first $50.00 of child support received in a month is disregarded in determining financial eligibility.
-- Child support in excess of $50.00 is counted as unearned income. If a unit is determined financially eligible, child support
-- is disregarded in determining the amount of the grant."
GIVEN `f` IS A `TANF family`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the unearned income counted for eligibility of` `f` MEANS
    `f`'s `unearned income other than child support` PLUS max 0 (`f`'s `child support received in the month` MINUS 50)

GIVEN `f` IS A `TANF family`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the gross income of` `f` MEANS
    sum (map `gross earnings` (`f`'s `earners`)) PLUS `the unearned income counted for eligibility of` `f`
    WHERE
        `gross earnings` `e` MEANS `e`'s `gross earned income in the month`

GIVEN `f` IS A `TANF family`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the applicant net income of` `f` MEANS
    sum (map `net` (`f`'s `earners`)) PLUS `the unearned income counted for eligibility of` `f`
    WHERE
        `net` `e` MEANS `the applicant-test net earnings of` `e`

GIVEN `f` IS A `TANF family`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the net income counting child support, after all disregards, of` `f` MEANS
    sum (map `net` (`f`'s `earners`)) PLUS `the unearned income counted for eligibility of` `f`
    WHERE
        `net` `e` MEANS `the net earnings after all disregards of` `e`

-- For the grant, child support is disregarded altogether (DSSM 4005.1).
GIVEN `f` IS A `TANF family`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the net income for the grant of` `f` MEANS
    sum (map `net` (`f`'s `earners`)) PLUS `f`'s `unearned income other than child support`
    WHERE
        `net` `e` MEANS `the net earnings after all disregards of` `e`

§§ `DSSM 4008 -- the income tests`

-- 4008.1.1 / 4008.1.2 Step 1: "Deny assistance if the income exceeds 185% of the applicable ... standard of need."
GIVEN `f` IS A `TANF family`
      `s` IS A `TANF standards`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the family passes the gross income test` IF
    `the gross income of` `f` AT MOST `s`'s `185% of the standard of need`

-- 4008.1.1 Step 2 (applicants): "Compare the net income to the payment standard. Deny assistance if the income exceeds the
-- payment standard." 4008.1.2 Step 2 (recipients): "Deny assistance if the income exceeds the standard of need."
-- The steps deny only where income "exceeds"; 4008's overview says income "must be less than" the limits. The steps are
-- followed (NOTES.md finding 3).
GIVEN `f` IS A `TANF family`
      `s` IS A `TANF standards`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the family passes the net income test` IF
    IF   `f`'s `an applicant, not a recipient`
    THEN `the applicant net income of` `f` AT MOST `s`'s `payment standard`
    ELSE `the net income counting child support, after all disregards, of` `f` AT MOST `s`'s `standard of need`

§§ `Eligibility on the tests encoded`

-- s 503(a): "Assistance shall not be granted ... to any person or family otherwise eligible ..., having conveyed or transferred
-- real or personal property of a value of $500 or more without fair consideration within 2 years preceding the date of
-- application for assistance or subsequently while receiving assistance, or to any person who is an inmate of any public
-- institution (except as a patient in a medical institution)." s 503(d): "In order to receive assistance under this
-- subsection, the parent, guardian or persons standing in loco parentis to a dependent child must have instituted suit for
-- nonsupport in the Family Court or must cooperate with the Department ... for the purpose of instituting proceedings for
-- nonsupport". DSSM 4002.2: "A family budget group is not eligible for TANF if its available resources exceed $10,000.00."
GIVEN `f` IS A `TANF family`
      `s` IS A `TANF standards`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the family is eligible for TANF, on the tests encoded` IF
        (NOT `f`'s `transferred property worth $500 or more without fair consideration within 2 years before applying, or since`)
    AND (NOT `f`'s `an inmate of a public institution, other than a patient in a medical institution`)
    AND `f`'s `has sued for nonsupport or cooperates with the Department to do so`
    AND `f`'s `available resources` AT MOST 10000
    AND `the family passes the gross income test` `f` `s`
    AND `the family passes the net income test` `f` `s`

§§ `DSSM 4007, 4008 -- the grant (Fill the Gap)`

-- 4008.1.1 Step 3 and 4008.1.2 Step 3: "Subtract the net income from the applicable standard of need; the number calculated is
-- the deficit. Multiply the deficit by 50%; the number calculated is the remainder. The grant is either the remainder or the
-- payment standard whichever is less." DSSM 4007: "Grants are not issued in amounts less than $10.00." No rounding is stated
-- for TANF (NOTES.md finding 4).
GIVEN `f` IS A `TANF family`
      `s` IS A `TANF standards`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the TANF grant for` `f` `with standards` `s` MEANS
    IF   `the family is eligible for TANF, on the tests encoded` `f` `s` AND `the grant` AT LEAST 10
    THEN `the grant`
    ELSE 0
    WHERE
        `the deficit` MEANS max 0 (`s`'s `standard of need` MINUS `the net income for the grant of` `f`)
        `the remainder` MEANS 50% TIMES `the deficit`
        `the grant` MEANS min `the remainder` (`s`'s `payment standard`)

§§ `Duties and rights`

DECLARE `TANF party` IS ONE OF
    `the recipient`
    `the applicant or recipient`

DECLARE `TANF action` IS ONE OF
    `notify the Department of the property or income`
    `appeal the hearing decision to the Superior Court`

-- s 510: "If at any time during the period assistance payments are being made to any person, such person becomes possessed of
-- any property, real or personal, or of any income in excess of the amount of such property and income last declared by such
-- person to the Department, such person shall notify the Department promptly ... Any excess paid to any person by reason of
-- such person's failure to report as required by this section shall be recoverable in a civil action". "Promptly" has no
-- number, so the rule has no WITHIN: a failure shows only as the excess the Department may recover.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `TANF party` `TANF action`
`the s 510 duty to report new property or income` MEANS
    PARTY  `the recipient`
    MUST   `notify the Department of the property or income`
    HENCE  FULFILLED

-- s 520: "Any applicant for or recipient of public assistance benefits ... against whom an administrative hearing decision has
-- been decided may appeal such decision to the Superior Court if the decision would result in financial harm to the
-- appellant. The appeal shall be filed within 30 days of the day of the final administrative decision." An appeal not filed
-- is no breach (DO ... LEST FULFILLED; in the stable l4 a MAY would take its HENCE when the time runs out unused).
GIVETH A DEONTIC `TANF party` `TANF action`
`the s 520 right to appeal` MEANS
    PARTY  `the applicant or recipient`
    DO     `appeal the hearing decision to the Superior Court`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   FULFILLED

§ `Questions for the applicant`

§§ `The standards`

@export What are Delaware's TANF standards for a family of this size, as printed in DSSM 4007.2 (dated 10/2002 - 9/2003)?
GIVEN `people in my family's budget` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people are in your family budget group (whose needs and income are counted together)
GIVETH A `TANF standards`
`What are the TANF standards for my family` MEANS `the DSSM 4007.2 standards for` `people in my family's budget`

§§ `Does my family qualify?`

@export Does my family pass Delaware's TANF tests this month: resources, the 185% gross income test and the net income test (31 Del. C. s 503, DSSM 4002.2, 4008)?
GIVEN `people in my family's budget` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people are in your family budget group
      `we are applying, not already receiving` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your family is applying and got no TANF in any of the four months before applying (an applicant), rather than receiving it now or in one of those months (a recipient)
      `my gross earnings this month` IS A NUMBER @desc Your gross wages or self-employment earnings this month, in US dollars (not your children's earnings, not EITC)
      `my disregard stage` IS A `Disregard stage` @desc Which earned-income disregard you are in: the four months of the $30 plus 1/3 disregard, the eight months of the $30 disregard, or past both
      `dependent care I pay for children under two` IS A NUMBER @desc What you pay this month for care of dependent children under two, in US dollars
      `children under two in care` IS A NUMBER @desc How many such children
      `dependent care I pay for other children or incapacitated adults` IS A NUMBER @desc What you pay this month for care of other dependent children or incapacitated adults, in US dollars
      `others in care` IS A NUMBER @desc How many such children or adults
      `our other unearned income` IS A NUMBER @desc Unearned income other than child support this month (for example Social Security, a pension, unemployment benefits), in US dollars
      `child support we received this month` IS A NUMBER @desc Child support your family received this month, in US dollars
      `our available resources` IS A NUMBER @desc Cash, bank accounts and other resources your family has on hand, in US dollars
      `we gave away property worth $500 or more in the last 2 years` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether anyone in the family transferred property worth $500 or more without fair payment in the 2 years before applying, or since
      `someone is an inmate of a public institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person needing assistance is an inmate of a public institution (not a patient in a medical institution)
      `we cooperate on child support` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have sued for nonsupport in Family Court, or cooperate with the Department to do so
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my family pass the TANF tests` IF
    `the family is eligible for TANF, on the tests encoded` `the family` (`the DSSM 4007.2 standards for` `people in my family's budget`)
    WHERE
        `the family` MEANS
            `TANF family` OF `people in my family's budget`, `we are applying, not already receiving`,
                             (LIST (`Earner` OF `my gross earnings this month`, `my disregard stage`,
                                                `dependent care I pay for children under two`, `children under two in care`,
                                                `dependent care I pay for other children or incapacitated adults`, `others in care`)),
                             `our other unearned income`, `child support we received this month`, `our available resources`,
                             `we gave away property worth $500 or more in the last 2 years`, `someone is an inmate of a public institution`,
                             `we cooperate on child support`

§§ `How much?`

@export How much would my family's monthly TANF grant be, with one wage earner and the standards printed in DSSM 4007.2 (DSSM 4008)?
GIVEN `people in my family's budget` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people are in your family budget group
      `we are applying, not already receiving` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your family is applying and got no TANF in any of the four months before applying
      `my gross earnings this month` IS A NUMBER @desc Your gross wages or self-employment earnings this month, in US dollars
      `my disregard stage` IS A `Disregard stage` @desc Which earned-income disregard you are in
      `dependent care I pay for children under two` IS A NUMBER @desc What you pay this month for care of dependent children under two, in US dollars
      `children under two in care` IS A NUMBER @desc How many such children
      `dependent care I pay for other children or incapacitated adults` IS A NUMBER @desc What you pay this month for care of other dependent children or incapacitated adults, in US dollars
      `others in care` IS A NUMBER @desc How many such children or adults
      `our other unearned income` IS A NUMBER @desc Unearned income other than child support this month, in US dollars
      `child support we received this month` IS A NUMBER @desc Child support your family received this month, in US dollars
      `our available resources` IS A NUMBER @desc Your family's available resources, in US dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much would our TANF grant be` MEANS
    `How much would our TANF grant be, with these standards` `people in my family's budget` `we are applying, not already receiving`
        `my gross earnings this month` `my disregard stage` `dependent care I pay for children under two` `children under two in care`
        `dependent care I pay for other children or incapacitated adults` `others in care` `our other unearned income`
        `child support we received this month` `our available resources`
        (`the DSSM 4007.2 standards for` `people in my family's budget`)

@export How much would my family's monthly TANF grant be, with one wage earner and the standards from the current COLA Administrative Notice (DSSM 4008)?
GIVEN `people in my family's budget` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people are in your family budget group
      `we are applying, not already receiving` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your family is applying and got no TANF in any of the four months before applying
      `my gross earnings this month` IS A NUMBER @desc Your gross wages or self-employment earnings this month, in US dollars
      `my disregard stage` IS A `Disregard stage` @desc Which earned-income disregard you are in
      `dependent care I pay for children under two` IS A NUMBER @desc What you pay this month for care of dependent children under two, in US dollars
      `children under two in care` IS A NUMBER @desc How many such children
      `dependent care I pay for other children or incapacitated adults` IS A NUMBER @desc What you pay this month for care of other dependent children or incapacitated adults, in US dollars
      `others in care` IS A NUMBER @desc How many such children or adults
      `our other unearned income` IS A NUMBER @desc Unearned income other than child support this month, in US dollars
      `child support we received this month` IS A NUMBER @desc Child support your family received this month, in US dollars
      `our available resources` IS A NUMBER @desc Your family's available resources, in US dollars
      `the standards` IS A `TANF standards` @desc The current 185% of the standard of need, standard of need and payment standard for your family's size, from the Division of Social Services' COLA Administrative Notice
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much would our TANF grant be, with these standards` MEANS
    `the TANF grant for` `the family` `with standards` `the standards`
    WHERE
        `the family` MEANS
            `TANF family` OF `people in my family's budget`, `we are applying, not already receiving`,
                             (LIST (`Earner` OF `my gross earnings this month`, `my disregard stage`,
                                                `dependent care I pay for children under two`, `children under two in care`,
                                                `dependent care I pay for other children or incapacitated adults`, `others in care`)),
                             `our other unearned income`, `child support we received this month`, `our available resources`,
                             FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
    -- the s 503(a), (d) facts are taken as not barring: the grant question assumes a family not barred on those grounds

§§ `Appeals`

@export Until what date may I appeal a TANF hearing decision to the Superior Court (31 Del. C. s 520)?
GIVEN `the day of the final administrative decision` IS A DATE @desc The day of the final administrative (hearing) decision
GIVETH A DATE
`Until when may I appeal to the Superior Court` MEANS `the day of the final administrative decision` PLUS 30

@export May I appeal this TANF hearing decision to the Superior Court (31 Del. C. s 520)?
GIVEN `the decision went against me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an administrative hearing decision on your TANF was decided against you
      `it would cause me financial harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decision would result in financial harm to you
      `the day of the final administrative decision` IS A DATE @desc The day of the final administrative decision
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I appeal to the Superior Court` IF
        `the decision went against me`
    AND `it would cause me financial harm`
    AND `today` AT MOST `Until when may I appeal to the Superior Court` `the day of the final administrative decision`
